      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr has inadequate oxygen resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6317005::chunk::001::introduction::42ad25eeb0",
        "PMC7513042::chunk::001::introduction::f13797f6f6"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature pack-cementation siliconizing can deposit an approximately 10–20 µm silicide layer on equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The siliconizing treatment will produce a continuous, uniform, and adherent silicide-derived surface layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The silicide-derived layer will convert to a silica barrier during oxidation in air at 800–1000 °C.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Silicon in the treated surface will oxidize preferentially during high-temperature air exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting SiO2 scale will be stable and have low oxygen permeability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiO2 scale will limit oxygen ingress into the bulk HfNbTaTiZr alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting oxygen ingress will reduce oxidation-related degradation and pesting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Siliconized HfNbTaTiZr will exhibit less oxidation, oxide-scale spallation, and pesting than untreated HfNbTaTiZr after 5 hours in air at 800–1000 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Siliconized HfNbTaTiZr will retain room-temperature ductility better than untreated material after the specified exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Siliconized HfNbTaTiZr will retain high-temperature yield strength better than untreated material after the specified exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr undergoes pesting and associated mechanical degradation under similar conditions.",
      "field": "baseline",
